20:    compounds. Aloe vera gel is applied to fruits as an edible coating which has been widely used for most fruits and
21:    vegetables. The aim of this work was to analyze the effects of biodegradable Aloe vera gel (aloe alone,1:1,1:2) along with
22:    1% pectin or CMC coating on tomato stored at room temperature. Matured leaves of Aloe vera plants were harvested and
23:    washed and gel was extracted. The viscosity of Aloe vera gel and its coating efficiency was improved by using 1%
25:    three different concentrations i.e., alone alone, 1:1(200 ml of Aloe vera gel: 200 ml of water), 1:2 (133.3 ml of Aloe vera gel:
26:    266.6 ml of water). The matured tomatoes (80%) were dipped in the coating solutions at room temperature for 10 min. At
27:    regular intervals, the fruits were rotated to increase the coating efficiency. They were allowed to drain for 2 min and then
30:    at room temperature. The results revealed aloe gel coating to be very beneficial in reducing the weight loss, minimizing
32:    result showed that the Aloe vera gel coatings along with CMC and pectin is effective in extending the shelf-life of tomato
