wiki/sources/zolfaghari2018-iran-wetlands-fish-mercury-lead.md:35:Mercury: all species below FAO, WHO, FDA, and EU limits. Lead: S. altidorsalis and S. zardunyi exceeded WHO and TAL limits; C. idella, C. carpio, H. molitrix below all regulatory limits. Maximum Allowable Fish Consumption Rate for mercury was highest for Hemiculter leucisculus. Lead HQ values: no HQ > 1 for any species from Hamun wetland, indicating no significant health risk from lead alone at measured concentrations. 20 fish samples per species. Mercury determined by Advanced Mercury Analyzer (LECO AMA 254 by ASTM D-6722); lead by AAS with graphite furnace (GBC GF 3000). Recovery for mercury standard reference materials: 95-100%.
